      name: "Ziprasidone", generic: "ziprasidone",
      aliases: ["Geodon", "ziprazidone", "ziprasidone hydrochloride", "qt antipsychotic", "antipsychotic take with 500 calories"],
      brandExamples: ["Geodon"],
      class: "Second-generation antipsychotic; D2/5-HT2A antagonist with prominent QT and food-dependent absorption",
      classPathway: ["Psychiatric medication", "Antipsychotic", "Second-generation antipsychotic", "QT-prolonging food-dependent benzisothiazolyl piperazine"],
      usedToTreat: "Adult schizophrenia; acute bipolar I manic/mixed episodes; bipolar I maintenance adjunct to lithium/valproate. Intramuscular formulation treats acute agitation in schizophrenia and has different administration rules.",
      description: "Ziprasidone blocks dopamine D2 and serotonin 5-HT2A receptors to treat schizophrenia and acute bipolar mania, with relatively low average weight/lipid burden but clinically important QT-prolongation risk. Oral absorption roughly doubles with food and should occur with a meal of about 500 calories; taking it without adequate food can create low, erratic exposure that looks like treatment failure. Lower metabolic burden therefore trades against meal adherence and cardiac-risk complexity rather than making ziprasidone universally safer.",
      mechanism: "D2 antagonism reduces mesolimbic psychosis and can cause EPS/prolactin effects; 5-HT2A antagonism modulates dopamine release. Ziprasidone also has 5-HT1A agonist and serotonin/norepinephrine transporter inhibitory activity that may contribute to mood effects. It blocks cardiac delayed-rectifier potassium current, slowing ventricular repolarization and increasing QTc; bradycardia, congenital long QT, structural heart disease, low potassium/magnesium and other QT drugs amplify torsades risk. Food increases bioavailability, so a missed meal changes pharmacokinetics more than a minor adherence detail.",
      boxedWarning: antipsychoticBox("Ziprasidone", "Its greater QT-prolonging capacity than several alternatives must influence drug selection. It is contraindicated in known QT prolongation, recent acute MI, uncompensated heart failure and specified QT-prolonging combinations."),
      adverseEffects: ["QT prolongation, palpitations, syncope and rare torsades", "Somnolence, dizziness, akathisia and other EPS", "Nausea and relatively modest average weight change", "NMS, tardive dyskinesia, DRESS and priapism"],
      contraindications: ["Known QT prolongation/congenital long-QT syndrome, recent acute MI or uncompensated heart failure", "Specified QT-prolonging drugs and product hypersensitivity", "Correct clinically important low potassium/magnesium before treatment"],
      nursingEssentials: ["Give every oral dose with an adequate meal and document whether apparent nonresponse follows fasting administration.", "Treat syncope, new palpitations or seizure-like collapse as a possible rhythm problem and obtain ECG/electrolyte assessment."],
      interactions: ["Other QT-prolonging drugs are contraindicated or should be avoided according to labeling.", "CYP3A4 inhibitors/inducers alter exposure, though QT risk remains the dominant interaction screen.", "Diuretics, vomiting and diarrhea increase risk through low potassium/magnesium."],
      keyLabs: ["ECG when cardiac risk exists", "Potassium and magnesium before/through treatment when depletion risk exists", "AIMS/EPS and standard metabolic monitoring"],
      nclexTraps: ["Lower metabolic risk does not mean lower overall risk.", "A dose swallowed without enough food may deliver much less drug.", "Syncope is not automatically orthostasis in a QT-prolonging drug."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("Pediatric safety/effectiveness vary and are not established for several formulations/indications.", "Cardiac disease, electrolyte loss, dementia mortality and falls narrow suitability.", "Late exposure can cause neonatal EPS/withdrawal; coordinate ECG/electrolyte and maternal relapse considerations."),
      sourceNote: "Current U.S. GEODON labeling: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=819997d8-e091-4081-85e1-bf50d39837ee",
      tags: ["frontier-wave5", "psychiatry", "ziprasidone", "Geodon", "second generation", "QT", "500 calories", "food"]
